\cf0 The floor violently shuddered.\
A deep, guttural roar vibrated through the floorboards as the oak table split in two. The floor beneath him tore open, sending jagged tiles tumbling into a blinding, orange abyss. A wave of unbearable heat hit his face as a pit of churning, molten lava roared to life directly under the kitchen footprint. Air turned thick with sulfur, and glowing embers erupted like fireworks, singeing his hair.\
Arthur didn't flinch. He didn't drop his fork. Living on a active volcanic ley-line had its distinct daily hazards, but he had a routine to keep.\
Hooking his knees around the legs of his chair, he leaned back over the roaring magma, balancing delicately on the remaining two inches of linoleum. The radiant heat from the molten lake below instantly toasted his sourdough to a flawless dark gold and crisp-charred the bacon in mid-air. He reached into the rising thermal updraft, snatched his hovering mug of coffee, and took a slow, deliberate sip.\
A bit more sulfurous than usual, perhaps, but the eggs were still perfectly cooked.\
